752-action each, alternatives as separate steps, no key name (the same fix is read in the detail, in
753-`scan_result` and in the README, and a key is true in only one of them), and the tool or the
754-Kubernetes version named when it decides the answer. A `Repro` is built only through `localRepro`
755-(or a wrapper of it such as `renderRepro`), never assembled by hand, so the `PlainWords` refusal, the
756-"no line from a container" rule and the "never copy `scan.tools.*.args`" rule always apply. Text written
757-by a third party (Trivy, plumber) is never restructured: it stays in `Resolution` as the scanner wrote
758-it.
759-
760-The reviewer checks this like the other rules; the techwriter is called in only to rewrite a text in
761-depth. Two tests in `internal/scan` hold what a machine can hold:
762-
763-- `steps_guard_test.go` reads every list a `*Steps` function of `steps.go` returns (inputs for each
764-  branch, in `stepSamples`; `TestEveryStepsFunctionHasASample` finds the functions by parsing
